menu "DirecSun bench options"

    config DIRECSUN_BENCH_STALL_TEST
        bool "Control-stall watchdog test hook (bench builds only)"
        default n
        help
            Bench check BC-5 (changes/3-teleop/R3.4-control-task.md): blocks the
            control task once, DIRECSUN_BENCH_STALL_AFTER_S seconds after it
            starts, for DIRECSUN_BENCH_STALL_MS milliseconds. The stall watchdog
            must reset the board within 100 ms. Never enable this in a flight
            build; firmware/sdkconfig.bench turns it on for the bench build only.

    config DIRECSUN_BENCH_STALL_AFTER_S
        int "Seconds after the control task starts"
        depends on DIRECSUN_BENCH_STALL_TEST
        default 10
        range 2 600

    config DIRECSUN_BENCH_STALL_MS
        int "Block duration in milliseconds"
        depends on DIRECSUN_BENCH_STALL_TEST
        default 200
        range 120 2000

    config DIRECSUN_BENCH_STAGE_TIMING
        bool "Per-stage control tick timing (bench diagnostic)"
        default n
        help
            Bench diagnostic for the control tick budget (R3.4): measures the
            longest time each stage of the tick took in every second (IMU burst,
            magnetometer poll, ADC read, Hall drain, estimator, supervisor,
            DShot frame, outbound queues, telemetry snapshot) and has the status
            task print one "stages" line per second. Adds a few esp_timer reads
            per tick; leave it off in flight builds. firmware/sdkconfig.diag
            turns it on.

endmenu
